import GromovWitten.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.EtaleSliceLocal

/-!
# Choosing the slicing functions: generation of the relative cotangent module

`Stacks.EtaleSliceLocal.etale_slice_specMap` makes an affine slice of a smooth morphism étale
*provided* `d` functions whose differentials generate the relative cotangent module are given.
This file produces those functions, with no hypothesis beyond unramifiedness of the pair.

The situation is the affine model of the local step of Stacks 06N3: `B` is an `A`-algebra through
`t^# = algebraMap A B`, standard smooth of relative dimension `d` (geometrically `A = 𝒪(U)`,
`B = 𝒪(R)` for a presentation `t, s : R ⇉ U` of an algebraic stack, `t` smooth of relative
dimension `d`), and `s : A →+* B` is a second ring map.  The pair `(t, s)` is the ring map
`A ⊗ A → B`, `a ⊗ a' ↦ t^# a * s a'`, whose image is the `A`-subalgebra `pairImage s` of `B`
generated by the image of `s`; since relative differentials only see the image of the base ring,
unramifiedness of `(t, s) : R ⟶ U ⨯ U` is the hypothesis
`Algebra.FormallyUnramified (pairImage s) B` used below.

## Main results

* `span_range_D_comp_eq_top`: if `B` is formally unramified over `pairImage s`, the differentials
  `d (s a)`, `a : A`, generate `Ω[B⁄A]` over `B`.  This is the "`Ω_{R/U ⨯ U} = 0` forces
  `s^*Ω_{U} ↠ Ω_{R/U}`" step, in the form needed for the slicing: *every* element of `Ω[B⁄A]` is a
  `B`-combination of differentials of functions pulled back along `s`.  `…_of_tower` is the same
  statement for an arbitrary intermediate ring, and `…_of_tensor` is the version whose hypothesis
  is formal unramifiedness over `A ⊗[R] A` itself.
* `cotangentBasis`: the relative cotangent module of a standard smooth algebra of relative
  dimension `d`, as a free module with basis indexed by `Fin d`.
* `exists_fin_span_sup_smul_eq_top`: **the choice of the slicing functions in the fibre.**  At a
  maximal ideal `q` of `B` there are `d` functions `f : Fin d → A` whose differentials
  `d (s (f i))` generate `Ω[B⁄A] ⊗ κ(q)`, i.e. generate `Ω[B⁄A]` modulo `q`.
* `exists_fin_notMem_smul_mem_span`: **the choice of the slicing functions near a prime.**  For any
  proper ideal `q` (in particular any prime, e.g. the one of the identity section `e (u)`) there
  are `f : Fin d → A` and `h ∉ q` with `h • Ω[B⁄A] ⊆ span {d (s (f i))}`, i.e. the `d (s (f i))`
  generate `Ω[B⁄A]` after inverting `h`.
* `exists_fin_notMem_smul_mem_span_of_formallyUnramified`: the two previous items combined — the
  unconditional generation statement, whose only hypotheses are standard smoothness of `t^#` of
  relative dimension `d` and formal unramifiedness of the pair `(t^#, s)`.
* `span_range_D_localizationAway_eq_top`: the transport of that conclusion to the localisation
  `B_h`, where the `d (s (f i))` generate `Ω[B_h⁄A]` on the nose — the missing bookkeeping step
  listed in `Stacks.EtaleSliceLocal`.
* `exists_etale_slice_specMap`: **the affine slice through a prime is étale.**  Combining the
  above with `EtaleSliceLocal.etale_slice_specMap`: for every prime `q` of `B` there are `d`
  functions `f : Fin d → A` and `h ∉ q` such that the slice morphism
  `Spec (A ⧸ (f)) ×_{Spec A} Spec B_h ⟶ Spec A` of the pair is étale.  This is the affine,
  unconditional form of the local step of Stacks 06N3.
* `eq_top_of_forall_isMaximal` and `etale_slice_specMap_of_forall_isMaximal`: the local-global
  complement.  If the *same* `d` functions generate the relative cotangent module modulo *every*
  maximal ideal of `B`, then the slice is étale on all of `Spec B`, with no localisation.  This
  isolates the one input the local step of Stacks 06N3 still needs beyond what is proved here.

What is *not* here: in `exists_etale_slice_specMap` the slice has been shrunk (`B` is replaced by
`B_h`), which is legitimate for a single point but is exactly what the covering condition of
`GromovWitten.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleSliceExists` forbids; see
`Stacks.EtaleSliceLocalSlicing` for the corrected covering condition
(`SaturatedEtaleSliceExists`) and for what the groupoid structure of `R = U ×_X U` must still
supply, namely that generation at the identity section propagates along the whole of `s⁻¹(W)`.
-/

open TensorProduct AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace GromovWitten.EtaleSliceGeneration

universe u

variable {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

/-- The image of the ring map `A ⊗ A → B`, `a ⊗ a' ↦ (algebraMap A B a) * s a'`, determined by the
structure map of the `A`-algebra `B` and a second ring map `s : A →+* B`: it is the `A`-subalgebra
of `B` generated by the image of `s`.  In the geometric situation of Stacks 06N3 this is the image
of `𝒪(U ⨯ U) → 𝒪(R)` for a pair of morphisms `t, s : R ⇉ U`, so formal unramifiedness of `B` over
`pairImage s` is exactly unramifiedness of `(t, s) : R ⟶ U ⨯ U` (relative differentials do not
change when the base ring is replaced by its image). -/
def pairImage (s : A →+* B) : Subalgebra A B :=
  Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range (s : A → B))

/-- Every function pulled back along `s` lies in `pairImage s`. -/
theorem apply_mem_pairImage (s : A →+* B) (a : A) : s a ∈ pairImage s :=
  Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨a, rfl⟩

/-- The differentials of the functions `s a` span the differentials of all of `pairImage s`: the
span is stable under the operations generating the subalgebra, by the Leibniz rule and because
differentials of elements of the base `A` vanish. -/
theorem D_mem_span_of_mem_pairImage (s : A →+* B) {b : B} (hb : b ∈ pairImage s) :
    KaehlerDifferential.D A B b ∈
      Submodule.span B (Set.range fun a : A ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s a)) := by
  have hb' : b ∈ Algebra.adjoin A (Set.range (s : A → B)) := hb
  clear hb
  induction hb' using Algebra.adjoin_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hx
      exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨a, rfl⟩
  | algebraMap r => simp
  | add x y _ _ ihx ihy => simpa using Submodule.add_mem _ ihx ihy
  | mul x y _ _ ihx ihy =>
      rw [Derivation.leibniz]
      exact Submodule.add_mem _ (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ ihy) (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ ihx)

/-- **Generation from an intermediate ring.**  Suppose `B` is formally unramified over an
intermediate `A`-algebra `S` — in the application `S` is `A ⊗ A`, or its image `pairImage s` in
`B` — and that the differentials of the elements of `S` lie in the span of the differentials of
the functions pulled back along `s`.  Then those differentials generate `Ω[B⁄A]`.

The proof is the relative cotangent sequence of `A → S → B`: unramifiedness kills `Ω[B⁄S]`, so
`B ⊗[S] Ω[S⁄A] → Ω[B⁄A]` is surjective
(`EtaleSlice.surjective_mapBaseChange_of_formallyUnramified`), and the source is spanned by the
`1 ⊗ d x`, `x : S`. -/
theorem span_range_D_comp_eq_top_of_tower (s : A →+* B) (S : Type u) [CommRing S] [Algebra A S]
    [Algebra S B] [IsScalarTower A S B] [Algebra.FormallyUnramified S B]
    (hS : ∀ x : S, KaehlerDifferential.D A B (algebraMap S B x) ∈
      Submodule.span B (Set.range fun a : A ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s a))) :
    Submodule.span B (Set.range fun a : A ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s a)) = ⊤ := by
  have h1 : Submodule.span B
      (Set.range fun x : S ↦ (1 : B) ⊗ₜ[S] KaehlerDifferential.D A S x) = ⊤ :=
    EtaleSliceLocal.span_tmul_eq_top_of_span_eq_top (C := B) (fun x : S ↦ x)
      (KaehlerDifferential.span_range_derivation A S)
  have h2 : Submodule.map (KaehlerDifferential.mapBaseChange A S B) ⊤ = ⊤ := by
    rw [Submodule.map_top, LinearMap.range_eq_top]
    exact EtaleSlice.surjective_mapBaseChange_of_formallyUnramified
  rw [← h1, Submodule.map_span, ← Set.range_comp] at h2
  refine top_unique ?_
  rw [← h2, Submodule.span_le]
  rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
  simp only [Function.comp_apply, KaehlerDifferential.mapBaseChange_tmul,
    KaehlerDifferential.map_D, one_smul]
  exact hS x

/-- **The differentials of the pullbacks `s a` generate the relative cotangent module.**  If `B` is
formally unramified over the subalgebra `pairImage s` generated by the image of `s` — the
ring-theoretic form of "the pair `(t, s) : R ⟶ U ⨯ U` is unramified" — then `Ω[B⁄A]` is generated
over `B` by the differentials `d (s a)`, `a : A`.  This is the first half of the choice of slicing
functions in Stacks 06N3. -/
theorem span_range_D_comp_eq_top (s : A →+* B) [Algebra.FormallyUnramified (pairImage s) B] :
    Submodule.span B (Set.range fun a : A ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s a)) = ⊤ :=
  span_range_D_comp_eq_top_of_tower s (pairImage s) fun x ↦ D_mem_span_of_mem_pairImage s x.2

/-- **Generation from unramifiedness over `A ⊗ A`.**  The geometric hypothesis of Stacks 06N3 is
that the pair `(t, s) : R ⟶ U ⨯ U` is unramified, i.e. that `B` is formally unramified over
`A ⊗[R] A` through the ring map `a ⊗ a' ↦ t^# a * s a'`; `hs` says that the given `s` is the
second factor of that map (the first one is `algebraMap A B` by `IsScalarTower`).  Then the
differentials `d (s a)` generate `Ω[B⁄A]`. -/
theorem span_range_D_comp_eq_top_of_tensor (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [Algebra R A] (s : A →+* B)
    [Algebra (A ⊗[R] A) B] [IsScalarTower A (A ⊗[R] A) B]
    [Algebra.FormallyUnramified (A ⊗[R] A) B]
    (hs : ∀ a : A, algebraMap (A ⊗[R] A) B ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] a) = s a) :
    Submodule.span B (Set.range fun a : A ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s a)) = ⊤ := by
  have ht : ∀ a : A, algebraMap (A ⊗[R] A) B (a ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : A)) = algebraMap A B a := by
    intro a
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A (A ⊗[R] A) B a]
    rfl
  refine span_range_D_comp_eq_top_of_tower s (A ⊗[R] A) fun x ↦ ?_
  induction x using TensorProduct.induction_on with
  | zero => simp
  | tmul a a' =>
      have hmul : (a ⊗ₜ[R] a' : A ⊗[R] A) = (a ⊗ₜ[R] (1 : A)) * ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] a') := by
        rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul, mul_one, one_mul]
      rw [hmul, map_mul, ht, hs, Derivation.leibniz]
      refine Submodule.add_mem _ (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨a', rfl⟩)) ?_
      simp
  | add x y hx hy =>
      rw [map_add, map_add]
      exact Submodule.add_mem _ hx hy

/-- The relative cotangent module of a standard smooth algebra of relative dimension `d`, as a
free module with basis indexed by `Fin d`. -/
noncomputable def cotangentBasis (d : ℕ) [Nontrivial B]
    [Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension d A B] : Module.Basis (Fin d) B Ω[B⁄A] :=
  haveI : Algebra.IsStandardSmooth A B :=
    Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension.isStandardSmooth d
  Module.finBasisOfFinrankEq B Ω[B⁄A] (Module.finrank_eq_of_rank_eq
    (Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension.rank_kaehlerDifferential d))

/-- **Choice of the slicing functions in a fibre.**  Let `B` be standard smooth over `A` of
relative dimension `d` and assume the differentials of the functions pulled back along
`s : A →+* B` generate `Ω[B⁄A]` (as `span_range_D_comp_eq_top` provides).  Then at every maximal
ideal `q` of `B` one can pick `d` functions `f : Fin d → A` whose differentials `d (s (f i))`
generate `Ω[B⁄A]` modulo `q`, i.e. generate the fibre `Ω[B⁄A] ⊗ κ(q)`: the fibre is a
`κ(q)`-vector space of dimension `d` spanned by the images of the `d (s a)`. -/
theorem exists_fin_span_sup_smul_eq_top (s : A →+* B) (d : ℕ) [Nontrivial B]
    [Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension d A B]
    (hgen : Submodule.span B (Set.range fun a : A ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s a)) = ⊤)
    (q : Ideal B) [q.IsMaximal] :
    ∃ f : Fin d → A,
      Submodule.span B (Set.range fun i ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s (f i))) ⊔
        q • (⊤ : Submodule B Ω[B⁄A]) = ⊤ := by
  obtain ⟨y, hyS, hy⟩ := EtaleSliceLocal.exists_subfamily_span_sup_smul_eq_top
    (cotangentBasis d) (Set.range fun a : A ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s a)) hgen q
  choose f hf using hyS
  refine ⟨f, ?_⟩
  have hfy : (fun i ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s (f i))) = y := funext hf
  rw [hfy]
  exact hy

/-- **Choice of the slicing functions near a prime.**  In the situation of
`exists_fin_span_sup_smul_eq_top`, but at an arbitrary proper ideal `q` of `B` — in the
application the prime of the point `e (u)` of the identity section — there are `d` functions
`f : Fin d → A` and an element `h ∉ q` such that the differentials `d (s (f i))` generate
`Ω[B⁄A]` after inverting `h`, in the spreading-out form `h • Ω[B⁄A] ⊆ span {d (s (f i))}`.

Passing to a maximal ideal `q ≤ m` is harmless: an element outside `m` is outside `q`. -/
theorem exists_fin_notMem_smul_mem_span (s : A →+* B) (d : ℕ) [Nontrivial B]
    [Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension d A B]
    (hgen : Submodule.span B (Set.range fun a : A ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s a)) = ⊤)
    (q : Ideal B) (hq : q ≠ ⊤) :
    ∃ (f : Fin d → A) (h : B), h ∉ q ∧ ∀ ω : Ω[B⁄A],
      h • ω ∈ Submodule.span B (Set.range fun i ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s (f i))) := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm, hle⟩ := q.exists_le_maximal hq
  have _ : m.IsMaximal := hm
  obtain ⟨y, h, hyS, hh, hh'⟩ := EtaleSliceLocal.exists_subfamily_notMem_smul_mem_span
    (cotangentBasis d) (Set.range fun a : A ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s a)) hgen m
  choose f hf using hyS
  refine ⟨f, h, fun hmem ↦ hh (hle hmem), ?_⟩
  have hfy : (fun i ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s (f i))) = y := funext hf
  rw [hfy]
  exact hh'

/-- **The slicing functions exist, unconditionally.**  Let `B` be an `A`-algebra which is standard
smooth of relative dimension `d`, let `s : A →+* B` be a second ring map, and assume the pair
is unramified, i.e. `B` is formally unramified over the subalgebra `pairImage s` generated by the
image of `s`.  Then for every proper ideal `q` of `B` there are `d` functions `f : Fin d → A` and
an element `h ∉ q` such that the differentials `d (s (f i))` generate `Ω[B⁄A]` after inverting
`h`.  These are the `d` functions by which Stacks 06N3 slices the chart. -/
theorem exists_fin_notMem_smul_mem_span_of_formallyUnramified (s : A →+* B) (d : ℕ)
    [Nontrivial B] [Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension d A B]
    [Algebra.FormallyUnramified (pairImage s) B] (q : Ideal B) (hq : q ≠ ⊤) :
    ∃ (f : Fin d → A) (h : B), h ∉ q ∧ ∀ ω : Ω[B⁄A],
      h • ω ∈ Submodule.span B (Set.range fun i ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s (f i))) :=
  exists_fin_notMem_smul_mem_span s d (span_range_D_comp_eq_top s) q hq

/-! ## From generation after inverting `h` to étaleness of the slice -/

section Localization

variable {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

/-- If an element `u` of the base ring becomes a unit in `S`, then a submodule over `S` containing
`u • x` contains `x`. -/
theorem mem_of_smul_mem_of_isUnit {R S M : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module S M] [IsScalarTower R S M] (P : Submodule S M) {u : R}
    (hu : IsUnit (algebraMap R S u)) {x : M} (hx : u • x ∈ P) : x ∈ P := by
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := hu
  have hx' : (algebraMap R S u) • x ∈ P := by rwa [algebraMap_smul]
  have hmem := P.smul_mem ((v⁻¹ : Sˣ) : S) hx'
  rwa [smul_smul, ← hv, ← Units.val_mul, inv_mul_cancel, Units.val_one, one_smul] at hmem

/-- **The chosen differentials generate the relative cotangent module after inverting `h`.**  If
`h • Ω[B⁄A]` is contained in the span of the differentials `d (s (f i))` — the conclusion of
`exists_fin_notMem_smul_mem_span` — then over the localisation `B_h` the differentials of the
images of the `f i` generate `Ω[B_h⁄A]`, which is the hypothesis `hspan` of
`EtaleSliceLocal.etale_slice_specMap`.

`Ω[B_h⁄A]` is the localisation of `Ω[B⁄A]` at the powers of `h`, so every element is of the form
`t⁻¹ • (image of ω)` with `t` a power of `h`; `h` and `t` are units in `B_h`, so the two
divisions are harmless. -/
theorem span_range_D_localizationAway_eq_top (s : A →+* B) {n : ℕ} (f : Fin n → A) (h : B)
    (hspanB : ∀ ω : Ω[B⁄A],
      h • ω ∈ Submodule.span B (Set.range fun i ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s (f i)))) :
    Submodule.span (Localization.Away h) (Set.range fun i ↦
      KaehlerDifferential.D A (Localization.Away h)
        (algebraMap B (Localization.Away h) (s (f i)))) = ⊤ := by
  have hle : Submodule.span B (Set.range fun i ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s (f i))) ≤
      Submodule.comap (KaehlerDifferential.map A A B (Localization.Away h))
        ((Submodule.span (Localization.Away h) (Set.range fun i ↦
          KaehlerDifferential.D A (Localization.Away h)
            (algebraMap B (Localization.Away h) (s (f i))))).restrictScalars B) := by
    rw [Submodule.span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    simp only [SetLike.mem_coe, Submodule.mem_comap, Submodule.restrictScalars_mem,
      KaehlerDifferential.map_D]
    exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩
  have key : ∀ ω : Ω[B⁄A], KaehlerDifferential.map A A B (Localization.Away h) ω ∈
      Submodule.span (Localization.Away h) (Set.range fun i ↦
        KaehlerDifferential.D A (Localization.Away h)
          (algebraMap B (Localization.Away h) (s (f i)))) := by
    intro ω
    have h1 := hle (hspanB ω)
    rw [Submodule.mem_comap, Submodule.restrictScalars_mem, map_smul] at h1
    exact mem_of_smul_mem_of_isUnit _
      (IsLocalization.map_units (M := Submonoid.powers h) _ ⟨h, Submonoid.mem_powers h⟩) h1
  refine top_unique fun ξ _ ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨⟨ω, t⟩, hty⟩ := IsLocalizedModule.surj (Submonoid.powers h)
    (KaehlerDifferential.map A A B (Localization.Away h)) ξ
  refine mem_of_smul_mem_of_isUnit _ (IsLocalization.map_units _ t) ?_
  have hty' : (t : B) • ξ = KaehlerDifferential.map A A B (Localization.Away h) ω := hty
  rw [hty']
  exact key ω

/-- **The slice of a standard smooth morphism through a prime is étale.**  Let `B` be an
`A`-algebra which is standard smooth of relative dimension `d`, let `s : A →+* B` be a second ring
map, and assume the pair is unramified, i.e. `B` is formally unramified over the subalgebra
`pairImage s`.  Then for every prime `q` of `B` — in the application the prime of the point `e (u)`
of the identity section — there are `d` functions `f : Fin d → A` cutting out a closed subscheme
`W = Spec (A ⧸ (f))` of `Spec A` and an element `h ∉ q` such that the slice morphism
`W ×_{Spec A} Spec B_h ⟶ Spec A` of the pair is étale.  This is the affine, unconditional form of
the local step of Stacks 06N3. -/
theorem exists_etale_slice_specMap (s : A →+* B) (d : ℕ) [Nontrivial B]
    [Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension d A B]
    [Algebra.FormallyUnramified (pairImage s) B] (q : Ideal B) [hq : q.IsPrime] :
    ∃ (f : Fin d → A) (h : B), h ∉ q ∧
      _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.Etale (CategoryTheory.Limits.pullback.snd
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span (Set.range f)))))
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom ((algebraMap B (Localization.Away h)).comp s))) ≫
          Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A (Localization.Away h)))) := by
  obtain ⟨f, h, hh, hspanB⟩ :=
    exists_fin_notMem_smul_mem_span_of_formallyUnramified s d q hq.ne_top
  refine ⟨f, h, hh, ?_⟩
  have hnt : Nontrivial (Localization.Away h) := by
    rw [← not_subsingleton_iff_nontrivial,
      IsLocalization.subsingleton_iff (M := Submonoid.powers h)]
    rintro ⟨m, hm⟩
    refine hh (hq.mem_of_pow_mem m ?_)
    have hm' : h ^ m = 0 := hm
    rw [hm']
    exact q.zero_mem
  have _ : Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension 0 B (Localization.Away h) :=
    Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension.localization_away h
  have _ : Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension d A (Localization.Away h) := by
    have htr := Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension.trans d 0 A B (Localization.Away h)
    rwa [zero_add] at htr
  have hI : (Ideal.span (Set.range f)).map ((algebraMap B (Localization.Away h)).comp s) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ algebraMap B (Localization.Away h) (s (f i))) := by
    rw [Ideal.map_span]
    congr 1
    exact (Set.range_comp _ f).symm
  exact EtaleSliceLocal.etale_slice_specMap d ((algebraMap B (Localization.Away h)).comp s)
    (Ideal.span (Set.range f)) (fun i ↦ algebraMap B (Localization.Away h) (s (f i))) hI
    (span_range_D_localizationAway_eq_top s f h hspanB)

end Localization

/-! ## Local-global: what makes the unlocalised slice étale -/

section LocalGlobal

variable {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

/-- **Local-global principle for generation.**  A submodule of a finitely generated module which is
everything modulo every maximal ideal is everything: the ideal `N.colon ⊤` of elements `b` with
`b • M ⊆ N` meets the complement of every maximal ideal by Nakayama
(`EtaleSliceLocal.exists_notMem_smul_mem_span`), hence is the unit ideal. -/
theorem eq_top_of_forall_isMaximal {M : Type u} [AddCommGroup M] [Module B M] [Module.Finite B M]
    (N : Submodule B M)
    (hN : ∀ q : Ideal B, q.IsMaximal → N ⊔ q • (⊤ : Submodule B M) = ⊤) : N = ⊤ := by
  have hspan : Submodule.span B (Set.range fun x : N ↦ (x : M)) = N := by simp
  have hcolon : N.colon (Set.univ : Set M) = ⊤ := by
    by_contra hne
    obtain ⟨q, hq, hle⟩ := (N.colon (Set.univ : Set M)).exists_le_maximal hne
    obtain ⟨u, hu, hu'⟩ := EtaleSliceLocal.exists_notMem_smul_mem_span
      (fun x : N ↦ (x : M)) q hq.ne_top (by rw [hspan]; exact hN q hq)
    refine hu (hle (Submodule.mem_colon.2 fun m _ ↦ ?_))
    rw [← hspan]
    exact hu' m
  refine top_unique fun x _ ↦ ?_
  have h1 : (1 : B) ∈ N.colon (Set.univ : Set M) := by
    rw [hcolon]
    exact Submodule.mem_top
  simpa using Submodule.mem_colon.1 h1 x (Set.mem_univ x)

/-- **The unlocalised affine slice is étale, given generation in every fibre.**  If `d` functions
`f : Fin d → A` have the property that their differentials `d (s (f i))` generate `Ω[B⁄A]` modulo
*every* maximal ideal of `B` — and not merely modulo the one of a chosen point, as
`exists_fin_span_sup_smul_eq_top` provides — then the slice morphism of the pair `(t, s)` cut out by
the `f i` is étale on all of `Spec B`, with no localisation: by
`eq_top_of_forall_isMaximal` the differentials then generate `Ω[B⁄A]` outright.

This isolates the precise remaining input of the local step of Stacks 06N3: the generation
condition has to hold at *every* point of `Spec B`, and it is the groupoid structure of
`R = U ×_X U` which propagates it from the identity section (see
`Stacks.EtaleSliceLocalSlicing`). -/
theorem etale_slice_specMap_of_forall_isMaximal (s : A →+* B) (d : ℕ) [Nontrivial B]
    [Algebra.IsStandardSmoothOfRelativeDimension d A B] (f : Fin d → A)
    (hf : ∀ q : Ideal B, q.IsMaximal →
      Submodule.span B (Set.range fun i ↦ KaehlerDifferential.D A B (s (f i))) ⊔
        q • (⊤ : Submodule B Ω[B⁄A]) = ⊤) :
    _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.Etale (CategoryTheory.Limits.pullback.snd
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span (Set.range f)))))
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom s)) ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A B))) := by
  have hI : (Ideal.span (Set.range f)).map s = Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ s (f i)) := by
    rw [Ideal.map_span]
    congr 1
    exact (Set.range_comp _ f).symm
  have _ : Module.Finite B Ω[B⁄A] := Module.Finite.of_basis (cotangentBasis d)
  exact EtaleSliceLocal.etale_slice_specMap d s (Ideal.span (Set.range f)) (fun i ↦ s (f i)) hI
    (eq_top_of_forall_isMaximal _ hf)

end LocalGlobal

